# A NUL byte in a source file made `git diff` treat it as binary and `grep`
# skip the file: `server/findings.ts` carried one as a hash separator for its
# whole life, so the rule it implemented was unreadable in the one place it was
# written, and a diff of it was unreviewable. The byte is gone (it is an escape
# now), and this says a source file is never binary whatever is inside it.
*.ts  diff
*.tsx diff
